# Database schema

- PostgreSQL 16 + Prisma 6 via `DATABASE_URL`. IDs `cuid()`. DateTime + `now()`. `updatedAt` `@updatedAt`.
- `WorkItem` maps to table `work_items`. Field `types` maps to column `labels_types` (`String[]`).
- Target: `Customer` + `Project.customerId` (nullable only during backfill, then NOT NULL). Cardinality Customer 1:N Project.
- Target GitLab: `GitLabProjectMapping` unique(instanceUrl, gitLabProjectId). `ExternalWorkItemReference` unique(provider, instance, project, issueId) and unique(workItemId) in phase one. Never store tokens in tables.
- TimeEntry workflow requires `workItemId`. `projectId` must match the WorkItem. Schema today allows nulls and does not enforce the pair — close this in API now, DB when ready.
- Set Decimal precision. Hours need fractional scale. Currency scale 2. Add checks: `hours > 0`, `progress BETWEEN 0 AND 100`.
- Do not put Developer/Infra/SA on `User.role`. Enforce one Company row per installation. `ProjectMember` stays unused by product.
- As-Is cascade: delete Project removes WorkItems/TimeEntries; delete WorkItem SetNulls `TimeEntry.workItemId`; delete User cascades TimeEntries. Add soft-delete/archive before history-destroying ops.
- Indexes from real queries (`projectId+status`, `role+status`, `TimeEntry(date)`, `customerId+status`). Measure first.
- Rollout: backup + restore test → additive nullable → backfill → validate → NOT NULL/unique. Prefer `db-push-safe`; versioned migrations when the team is ready.
- If multiple User rows exist, pick the owner with audit. Do not delete user rows until every FK is remapped.
